# Linker version script applied to libtriton.so when it is built with
# TRITON_EXT_ENABLED=1 (the plugin-compatible build, which exports Triton/MLIR/
# LLVM symbols with default visibility so out-of-tree plugins can resolve them).
#
# Problem it solves
# -----------------
# Triton loads a plugin via llvm::DynamicLibrary::getPermanentLibrary ->
# dlopen(RTLD_LAZY|RTLD_GLOBAL). The plugin DT_NEEDEDs libtriton.so, so that
# dlopen also promotes libtriton's symbols into the GLOBAL symbol scope. An
# EXT-enabled libtriton was compiled WITHOUT -fvisibility=hidden, so it exports
# not only Triton's API but also the incidental, weak C++ template
# instantiations the compiler emits for libstdc++ types
# (std::__cxx11::basic_string, std::vector, std::__detail regex internals, ...).
#
# Once those weak symbols are global they interpose the host process's identical
# symbols. PyTorch's pip wheels are built with the OLD libstdc++ ABI
# (_GLIBCXX_USE_CXX11_ABI=0) and against a different gcc than Triton's LLVM
# toolchain, so torch's std::regex (used by at::cuda::parseChosenWorkspaceSize to
# read CUBLAS_WORKSPACE_CONFIG) ends up calling libtriton's incompatible
# std::__cxx11::basic_string::_M_replace_aux on a torch-allocated string -> the
# SSO/heap bookkeeping disagrees and the first cuBLAS gemm aborts with
# `free(): invalid pointer`.
#
# Fix
# ---
# Keep exporting everything Triton needs for plugins, but force libtriton's
# libstdc++/libc++abi template instantiations to LOCAL binding so they can never
# interpose the host's. A version script with only a `local:` section leaves all
# other (Triton/MLIR/LLVM) symbols at their default (exported) binding.
#
# NOTE: only member/free FUNCTION instantiations are localized. We deliberately
# do NOT localize std:: typeinfo / vtable symbols (_ZTISt*, _ZTSSt*, _ZTVSt*):
# those identify exception types across shared-library boundaries (RTTI is
# matched by symbol address), and hiding them would break catching std
# exceptions thrown across the libtriton boundary.
{
  local:
    # std:: member/free functions (both the C++11 __cxx11 and the legacy COW
    # "Ss" manglings); excludes _ZTISt*/_ZTSSt*/_ZTVSt* (RTTI) by construction.
    _ZNSt*;
    _ZNKSt*;
    _ZSt*;
    _ZNSs*;
    _ZNKSs*;
    _ZStL*;
    # __gnu_cxx:: helpers
    _ZN9__gnu_cxx*;
    _ZNK9__gnu_cxx*;
    # libstdc++ basic_string helpers (the specific interposers we observed)
    *_M_replace_aux*;
    *_M_create*;
    *_M_mutate*;
};
